#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0252-A expect=violation domain=ADAE
#note "Isolates the `var_exists(\"BASECAyN\")` arm. AVALCA2N is NOT declared; the single expansion (y=2) is seeded by BASECA2N with AVALCA2N synthesised as an absent column, so it is the SECOND disjunct that fires. Dataset granularity -> exactly one violation for the two rows, reported at row=1. BASECA2N is pinned because it is present and its value comes from data row 1; AVALCA2N is deliberately NOT pinned - an unresolved output variable is omitted from the value map entirely."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 BASECA2N=1
dataset ADAE structure=OCCDS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col AEDECOD  type=Char
col BASECA2N type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | HEADACHE | 1
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | NAUSEA | 2
